WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.500
Born into two worlds—
one loving,

2
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:25.240
one chaotic.
And I was laid

3
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.000
right in the middle.

4
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.230
Soft hands wrapped me in a blanket,
Mother's breath against my brow.

5
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:51.000
She was tired, bent, and trembling,
Still she would not put me down.

6
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.110
One world moved in patient whispers,
Warm light resting on my skin.

7
00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:04.000
The other waited in the doorway
Like a storm already in.

8
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.270
I had no words to call it anger,
No way to understand.

9
00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:17.000
Only heartbeats, doors, and shadows—
And my mother's shielding hands.

10
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:24.270
I was born between two worlds,
One was mercy, one was war.

11
00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:31.800
One side rocked me through the crying,
One side rattled every door.

12
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.000
I was born between two worlds,
A little ghost beneath the light.

13
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:44.000
Love kept watch above my cradle
While rage thundered through the night.

14
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:52.000
And I lay there in the middle,
Too small to choose a side—

15
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Just Baby GhostHeart breathing,
Trying only to survive.

16
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:09.000
Boxes stacked beside my cradle,
New walls over where I slept.

17
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:18.000
Father's anger filled the hallway,
Mother held me while she wept.

18
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:25.000
Jail doors closed and jail doors opened—
He was gone, then back again.

19
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.000
I could only feel the weather;
I was too small to name the wind.

20
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:35.000
I won't remember every ceiling,
Every room or every fight.

21
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:42.000
But a baby's body listens
When the walls erupt at night.

22
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:49.000
I was born between two worlds,
One was mercy, one was war.

23
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:57.000
One side rocked me through the crying,
One side rattled every door.

24
00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:05.000
I was born between two worlds,
A little ghost beneath the light.

25
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Love kept watch above my cradle
While rage thundered through the night.

26
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:20.000
And I lay there in the middle,
Too small to choose a side—

27
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:28.000
Just Baby GhostHeart breathing,
Trying only to survive.

28
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:36.000
At my mother's parents' doorway,
Even breathing settled slow.

29
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Grandma's hands were calm and steady;
Grandpa made the whole room home.

30
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:52.000
No one made the windows tremble.
No one set the air aflame.

31
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:59.000
Only there, the night stayed gentle
Long enough to sleep again.

32
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:06.000
That was my one place of safety,
Where the storm could not get in.

33
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Their love became the quiet
Wrapped around my fragile skin.

34
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:20.000
I was not the fight around me.
I was not the reason why.

35
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:26.000
I was only Baby GhostHeart
Underneath a divided sky.

36
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Before memory, there was feeling.
Before language, there was sound.

37
00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:43.000
Before fire, just an ember
In a heart they couldn't drown.

38
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:50.000
I was born between two worlds,
One was mercy, one was war.

39
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:57.000
One side held me with its patience,
One side shook the walls and doors.

40
00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:04.000
I was born between two worlds,
A cracked heart barely giving light.

41
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:11.000
Love kept watch above my cradle
Through the anger of the night.

42
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:19.000
And I stayed there in the middle—
No voice, no place to hide.

43
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:27.000
Just Baby GhostHeart breathing,
With one ember still alive.

44
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:33.000
No clear memories.
Only echoes.

45
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.000
My mother's arms.

46
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:41.000
My grandparents' home.

47
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:44.000
A quiet room.

48
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.000
A closing door.

49
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.000
The fire had not awakened yet.

50
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:57.000
But it was there.
